    "result_text": "All 42 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors), including the three new Cp29 postcode tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional postcode support for owner creation. When a `postcode` is present it must be valid for the owner's city region; when absent the request stays backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`). Because `Owner` extends `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field appears on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), and MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` field (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to the `owners` table. (h2 is the active platform in tests.)\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added the fixed city\u2192region and region\u2192range tables and a `validatePostcode` method called during `addOwner`. It:\n   - passes silently when the postcode is absent/blank (optional),\n   - rejects with 400 (`InvalidRequestException`) when present but not exactly 4 digits,\n   - rejects with 400 when out of range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099),\n   - accepts any 4-digit value for a city with no known region.\n\nThe value is stored and returned exactly as given.",
